{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא כָּרַת וְגוֹ׳.</b> Its saying <b>נָתַתִּי</b> in the past tense is according to what has preceded us, that Abraham took possession of it, as we explained in its place (Genesis 13:15). It is therefore justified to say נָתַתִּי — I have already given — for the children will inherit by the law of inheritance." "<b>הִנֵּה</b> One must wonder how the eyes of those who refuse to believe in our future greatness and excellence are so blinded. For Scripture speaks explicitly, that YHWH cut a covenant with Abraham our father, peace be upon him, to give his seed ten nations, and until now we have not found that YHWH gave Israel more than seven nations, with three nations remaining. How then can the dry bones say (Ezekiel 37): our hope of inheritance is lost, and the oath of YHWH opposes them? Moreover, even the seven that YHWH gave did not all enter our grasp, and due to our sins slaves have ruled over us. And HaShem did this to allude to measure for measure: just as we are servants of YHWH yet do not submit to Him, blessed be He, like a slave rebelling against his master, so too the slaves who serve us will rebel against us. And yet further, the Almighty has words to fulfill His covenant." "Further, I set my heart to search through the order of the verses, and I saw that He placed first the Kenite and the Kenizzite and the Kadmonite — who are Ammon and Moab and Edom — which did not come into our hands first, but rather the seven later ones; and it is not proper to place the later before the earlier. But surely this was from before YHWH, to awaken you and to tell you that the essence of the giving is in the future, when the three shall come together along with the remainder of the seven nations, and [the mouth of iniquity] shall shut its mouth upon seeing the oath of YHWH. And a sign for the matter is the delivery of the four kings that YHWH gave to Abraham: three corresponding to Kenite and Kenizzite and Kadmonite, and the fourth was Tid'al king of goyim (Genesis 14:1) — an allusion to the assembling of the nations remaining among the first seven. Understand this:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :register {:flags {1 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:38.011775075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}